{"resourceIdentifier":"82","resourceName":"Wastewater Treatment with Biogas Production (UASB) and Heat Utilization at General Starch Co Ltd.","description":"The project activity involves installation of an anaerobic wastewater treatment facility, based on Upflow Anaerobic Sludge Blanket (UASB) technology, at a starch manufacturing plant that has been in operation since 1995. The first phase of the project (UASB 1) was implemented at General Starch Co., Ltd. in 2003 with start-up of operations in January 2004 and the second phase of the project (UASB 2) in 2005 with start-up of operations in January of 2006. The starch plant has a total production capacity of 600 tonnes of native starch per day, generating an average of 5,000 m3 of wastewater every production day. As a normal practice, the wastewater in the plant is treated through cascading lagoons with a retention time of more than a year. The minimum depth of these ponds is about 10 meters for the first two lagoons and more than 3 m from the water surface for the remaining lagoons.","location":{"latitude":14.343400,"longitude":102.636000},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"82"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Nakhorn Ratchasima Province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Papop Renewable Company Limited"},{"type":"string","value":"Bogotá D.C., Colombia"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"82"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"39411"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0014"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","